# Pinegrap - Enterprise Website Platform
#
# What docker/Dockerfile does not need from the repository. The image takes
# index.php, pinegrap/ and a few files of docker/; the development tree is
# left out of the build context.
#
# Of pinegrap/data/ only what the repository tracks goes in (the guard files,
# the default config template, the CA bundle and the two starter sites):
# everything else there belongs to an installation - a development machine's
# real config.php, its uploads and backups - and must never end up in an
# image layer.

.git
.github
.claude
CLAUDE.md
docs
tests
tools
dev
*.md
web.config
download_assistant.php
docker/.env

pinegrap/data/*
!pinegrap/data/.htaccess
!pinegrap/data/config(default).php
!pinegrap/data/cacert.pem
!pinegrap/data/files/.htaccess
!pinegrap/data/layouts/.htaccess
!pinegrap/data/temp/.htaccess
!pinegrap/data/backups/.htaccess
!pinegrap/data/backups/english_default
!pinegrap/data/backups/turkish_default

**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
